astrobench_a877243f10,astrobench_a877243f10_chunk_012,12,"In Section 5 we tackled the harder problem posedby flattened systemsby definingan auxiliary DF that satisfies the constraints near Jφ= 0, and then defining the DF to bea linear combinationof the original and auxiliary DFs that tendsto the auxiliary DF as Jφ→0. We showed thata com ponent with oneof these DFs that residesinan externally generated potential can have physically acceptable kinemat ics:σzis always less that σRwhileσφis smaller than σR at large radii but tendsto σRas the centreis approached. Moreover, in these models the vφdistributions don’t have cuspsat vφ= 0. We finishedby constructing self-consistent models with DFs that depend onJ=aJr+L, where aisa freepa rameter andL=Jz+|Jφ|. Whena/lessorequalslant1.4, the modelis radially biased, the bias increasingas adiminishes. To our surprise, all radially biased models provedtobe oblate – cal models. Concern that this resultisan artifact producedby useof the St¨ ackel Fudgeto evaluate actions was allayedby the near sphericityof the isochrone model that the code constructed from the isochrone’s known analytic ergodic DFf(J). The oblatenessof radially biased models withf(Jr,L) suggests that all radially biased spherical models are unsta bleto quadrupolar perturbations, but this possibility needstobe confirmedby",8 CONCLUSIONS,8 CONCLUSIONS,,,,,Distribution functions for spheroids,James Binney,astro-ph.GA,2026-02-26T15:41:51Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23127v1,2602.23127,distribution_functions,234,180,False,True,140,320,True,4.5
astrobench_a877243f10,astrobench_a877243f10_chunk_013,13,"system. Section 2 defines the problemtobe addressed. Section 3 investigatesit analytically. Section 4 solves the problem for spherical systems. Section 5 oﬀersa solution for flattened systems. Section 6 presents self-consistent models rather than components that are confinedbyan externally gen erated potential, finding that radial bias ina self-consist ent system flattens the even when its DF isf(Jr,L). Section 7 asks whether the conditionson fare still satisfied after the potential has been adiabatically deformed. Section 8 sumsup and suggests directions for further work.",1 INTRODUCTION Theextentandqualityofthedatathatareavailable for both,1 INTRODUCTION Theextentandqualityofthedatathatareavailable for both,,,,,Distribution functions for spheroids,James Binney,astro-ph.GA,2026-02-26T15:41:51Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23127v1,2602.23127,distribution_functions,106,81,False,False,700,781,True,4.0
