astrobench_3474c47fe1,astrobench_3474c47fe1_chunk_010,10,"Navarro 2001; Diemandetal. 2004; Ludlowetal. 2011; Svensmarketal. 2021); for galaxies and globular clusters theorbitalstructure showsalargerspreadin anisotropy(vandeVen etal.2006;Napolitanoetal.2014;Liepoldetal.2020;Santuccietal. 2022;Cohenetal.2021).Forthisreasonitisusefultoinvestigateto what extent our results canbe generalisedto more complex orbital structures. Theisotropicorbitalstructurecanbeconsideredasaspecialcaseof amoregeneralone-parameterfamilyoforbitalstructures,calledthe Osipkov–Merritt orbital structures (Osipkov 1979; Merritt 1985a). These models are characterised bya distribution function thatde pendson binding energy and angular momentum only through the combination𝑄=E−1 2𝜆𝐿2.Thevelocityanisotropyprofile,gener ally definedas 𝛽(𝑟)=1−𝜎2 𝜃 𝜎2𝑟,(12) hasa specific form for the Osipkov–Merritt models: 𝛽(𝑟)=𝜆𝑟2 1+𝜆𝑟2.(13) For𝜆=0,𝑄reduces toEand the Osipkov–Merritt orbital structure reducesto the isotropic one (𝛽=0). For𝜆 >0, the orbital struc ture varies from isotropicin the centreto purely radial (𝛽→1) at verylargeradii.ThistypeofOsipkov–MerrittmodeliscalledTypeI in Merritt (1985a) andis commonly adoptedin the literature (e.g. Merritt 1985b; Carolloetal. 1995; Ciotti & Lanzoni 1997; Widrow 2000; Łokas & Mamon 2001; Di Cintioetal. 2015; Di Cintio & Casetti 2020; Ciottietal. 2019). Finally, for𝜆<0, the orbital struc ture gradually changes from isotropicin the centreto completely tangential (𝛽→−∞) at𝑟=𝑟 a≡1/√ −𝜆. Theseso-called Type II Osipkov–Merritt models are only physically meaningful for spher ical models witha finite extent with𝑟 a⩽𝑟T, or equivalently with 𝜆⩾𝜆min=−1/𝑟2 T. Owingto this limitation, tangential Osipkov– Merritt models have only","4.2 Extensionto anisotropic orbital structures So farwe have focusedon isotropic dynamical models, the simplest","4.2 Extensionto anisotropic orbital structures So farwe have focusedon isotropic dynamical models, the simplest",,,,,Self-consistent dynamical m