astrobench_cbff59e329,astrobench_cbff59e329_chunk_000,0,"Kinematic diagnostics for non-axisymmetry in the Milky Way's nuclear stellar disc 2.1.The axisymmetric NSD model We adopt the axisymmetric, self-consistent dynamical modelof the NSD from Sormanietal. (2022)3. This model was fittedto 3https://github.com/GalacticDynamics-Oxford/Agama/ blob/master/py/example_mw_nsd.pythe line-of-sight and proper motion kinematic distributionsob tainedby combining the KMOS infrared (K-band) spectroscopic surveyof Fritzetal. (2021) witha preliminary versionof the VIRAC2 proper motion catalogue (Smithetal. 2025). The final fiducial NSD model hasa total mass ofM NSD=9.7×108M⊙, an exponential radial scale length ofR disc=74 pc anda vertical scale length ofH disc=26 pc.","2.1.The axisymmetric NSD model We adopt the axisymmetric, self-consistent dynamical modelof","2.1.The axisymmetric NSD model We adopt the axisymmetric, self-consistent dynamical modelof",,,,,Kinematic diagnostics for non-axisymmetry in the Milky Way's nuclear stellar disc,"Karl Fiteni, Xingchen Li, Mattia C. Sormani, Victor P. Debattista, Arianna Vasini, Francisco Nogueras-Lara, Jason L. Sanders, Nathan Deg, Mathias Schultheis, Marco Donati, Zi-Xuan Feng",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-19T10:39:35Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.18738v1,2603.18738,galactic_dynamics,110,84,False,True,0,84,True,5.0
astrobench_cbff59e329,astrobench_cbff59e329_chunk_001,1,"Kinematic diagnostics for non-axisymmetry in the Milky Way's nuclear stellar disc 2.2.The strong and weak NSB models To obtain isolated nuclear bar models, we evolve the isolated NSD modelof Sormanietal. (2022) within the self-consistent MW modelof Binney & Vasiliev (2023)4using theN-body code GADGET-4 (Springeletal. 2021). We use softening lengthsof 5, 50, and 25 pc for the NSD, dark matter, and main stellar disc components, respectively. We find that the initially axisymmet ric NSD is mildly unstable, and starts forminga nuclear bar after evolving for 0.6 Gyr. The left panelof Fig. 3, illustrates the evo lutionof theA 2bar amplitude, computed via the usualm=2 Fourier moment (e.g., Lietal. 2024), alongside the radius con taining 98% of the NSD’s mass (right panel). The output cadenceis sufficiently fine that theA 2profileis well-sampled across the full evolution; a running averageis appliedin Fig. 3 to reduce shot noise between successive outputs. The bar amplitude peaks att=1.7 Gyr, after whichit beginsto weaken. We extract two snapshots from this simulationto construct our barred NSD models: the strong NSB (S-NSB) att=1.70 Gyr (black dashed line) when the barisat peak","2.2.The strong and weak NSB models To obtain isolated nuclear bar models, we evolve the isolated","2.2.The strong and weak NSB models To obtain isolated nuclear bar models, we evolve the isolated",,,,,Kinematic diagnostics for non-axisymmetry in the Milky Way's nuclear stellar disc,"Karl Fiteni, Xingchen Li, Mattia C. Sormani, Victor P. Debattista, Arianna Vasini, Francisco Nogueras-Lara, Jason L. Sanders, Nathan Deg, Mathias Schultheis, Marco Donati, Zi-Xuan Feng",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-19T10:39:35Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.18738v1,2603.18738,galactic_dynamics,234,180,False,True,0,180,True,5.0
astrobench_cbff59e329,astrobench_cbff59e329_chunk_002,2,"Kinematic diagnostics for non-axisymmetry in the Milky Way's nuclear stellar disc 2.3.The large-scale MW model We employa self-consistentN-body+Smooth Particle Hydro dynamic (SPH) model ofa large-scale MW-like bar which cor respondsto the model TG07v3 in Degetal. (2025). Here, we provide onlya brief overview. The initial conditions consist ofa bulgeless stellar disc witha Sérsic surface density profile (Sérsic indexn=1.75), a gas disc 4https://github.com/GalacticDynamics-Oxford/Agama/ blob/master/py/example_self_consistent_model_mw.py Fig. 4: Plotsin Galactocentric Cartesian coordinatesof the isolated NSD (left), strong NSB (middle) and weak NSB (right) models orientedat−60◦relativeto the Sun-GC line. Overlaid are the velocity ellipses colouredby the vertex deviation,lv. We overlayan ellipsein each bin withN>25 stars. The dashed lines reflecta 2◦field-of-view centredon the Solar positionat (x,y)=(−8.2,0) kpc. The NSD shows radially oriented ellipses, while theS-NSB model ellipses show strong alignment with the bar’s major axis. The alignmentis weaker for theW-NSB model. (7% of the stellar mass), andan NFW dark matter halo (Navarroetal. 1997) with massMh=1.17×1012M⊙and scale radius Rh=19 kpc. The stellar disc hasa mass ofMd=5.5×1010M⊙ and scale lengthRd=0.43 kpc (for the Sérsic profile), while the gas disc hasan exponential scale length ofRg=6.5 kpc. The modelis evolved",2.3.The large-scale MW model We employa self-consistentN-body+Smooth Particle Hydro,2.3.The large-scale MW model We employa self-consistentN-body+Smooth Particle Hydro,,,,,Kinematic diagnostics for non-axisymmetry in the Milky Way's nuclear stellar disc,"Karl Fiteni, Xingchen Li, Mattia C. Sormani, Victor P. Debattista, Arianna Vasini, Francisco Nogueras-Lara, Jason L. Sanders, Nathan Deg, Mathias Schultheis, Marco Donati, Zi-Xuan Feng",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-19T10:39:35Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.18738v1,2603.18738,galactic_dynamics,234,180,False,True,0,180,True,4.5
astrobench_cbff59e329,astrobench_cbff59e329_chunk_003,3,"andan NFW dark matter halo (Navarroetal. 1997) with massMh=1.17×1012M⊙and scale radius Rh=19 kpc. The stellar disc hasa mass ofMd=5.5×1010M⊙ and scale lengthRd=0.43 kpc (for the Sérsic profile), while the gas disc hasan exponential scale length ofRg=6.5 kpc. The modelis evolved using Changa(Menonetal. 2015) for 10 Gyr usinga base timestepof∆t=0.5 Myr, which provides sufficient temporal resolution that our results are insensitiveto the choiceof output cadence. Star formation occurs when gas densityex ceeds 0.1 amucm−3and temperature falls below 15,000 K, witha star formation efficiencyof 5% per dynamical time and Super nova feedback via the Kelleretal. (2014) prescription. The resulting model developsa bar that reachesa stable con figurationby∼3.5 Gyr and remains approximately constant thereafter. Att=3 Gyr, the bar hasa semi-major radiusof Rbar∼4.25 kpc and pattern speed ofΩ∼42 kms−1kpc−1, con sistent with measurementsof the MW (e.g., Weggetal. 2015; Portailetal. 2017). The model also reproduces the characteris tic bimodal distributionof red clump stars observed along var ious linesof sight, mimicking the observed morphologyof the MW’s boxy/peanut bulge (Gonzalezetal. 2015). We note that this model does not includea metal-poor spheroidal stellar com ponentin the bulge; we",2.3.The large-scale MW model We employa self-consistentN-body+Smooth Particle Hydro,2.3.The large-scale MW model We employa self-consistentN-body+Smooth Particle Hydro,,,,,Kinematic diagnostics for non-axisymmetry in the Milky Way's nuclear stellar disc,"Karl Fiteni, Xingchen Li, Mattia C. Sormani, Victor P. Debattista, Arianna Vasini, Francisco Nogueras-Lara, Jason L. Sanders, Nathan Deg, Mathias Schultheis, Marco Donati, Zi-Xuan Feng",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-19T10:39:35Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.18738v1,2603.18738,galactic_dynamics,234,180,False,True,140,320,True,4.5
astrobench_cbff59e329,astrobench_cbff59e329_chunk_004,4,"the characteris tic bimodal distributionof red clump stars observed along var ious linesof sight, mimicking the observed morphologyof the MW’s boxy/peanut bulge (Gonzalezetal. 2015). We note that this model does not includea metal-poor spheroidal stellar com ponentin the bulge; we assess the potential impactof sucha populationin AppendixA and findit has negligible effecton our",2.3.The large-scale MW model We employa self-consistentN-body+Smooth Particle Hydro,2.3.The large-scale MW model We employa self-consistentN-body+Smooth Particle Hydro,,,,,Kinematic diagnostics for non-axisymmetry in the Milky Way's nuclear stellar disc,"Karl Fiteni, Xingchen Li, Mattia C. Sormani, Victor P. Debattista, Arianna Vasini, Francisco Nogueras-Lara, Jason L. Sanders, Nathan Deg, Mathias Schultheis, Marco Donati, Zi-Xuan Feng",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-19T10:39:35Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.18738v1,2603.18738,galactic_dynamics,69,53,False,False,280,333,True,4.0
