astrobench_b7b4f9944a,astrobench_b7b4f9944a_chunk_037,37,"−1.81×1010M⊙. Hence, including data whichisnotwellcapturedbythecurrentrigidMW–LMCsimulations can bias the inferencein the MW massby∼10%. As expected, the MW mass inferencefavours lower values when usingall data points becauseexcludedpointshavelowervelocitydispersions,whichprefer lower masses (Jeans 1915). Moreover, we find that the inferenceof the total masses for the MW,𝑀 200,MWand LMC,𝑀 LMC, givesa mass ratioof≈30±10%for the LMC’s infall massto the MW’s present day mass.","5.2 The massof the Milky Way and Large Magellanic Cloud Previously, in Brooksetal.(2025) we used the H3+SEGUE+MagE","5.2 The massof the Milky Way and Large Magellanic Cloud Previously, in Brooksetal.(2025) we used the H3+SEGUE+MagE",,,,,"Quantifying the Milky Way, LMC and their interaction using all-sky kinematics of outer halo stars","Richard A. N. Brooks, Jason L. Sanders, Adam M. Dillamore, Nicolás Garavito-Camargo, Vedant Chandra, Adrian M. Price-Whelan, Phillip Cargile",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-09T18:00:04Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.08788v1,2603.08788,galactic_dynamics,73,56,True,False,280,336,False,2.0
astrobench_b7b4f9944a,astrobench_b7b4f9944a_chunk_038,38,"shownas squares, colouredby the observational tracer used; blue for stellar streams, pink for Local Group, teal for satellites and yellow for LMC stars. The numerical values demonstrate the authors: 1 – vanderMarel&Kallivayalil(2014),2–Cullinaneetal.(2020),3–Watkinsetal. (2024), 4 – Warrenetal. (2025), 5/6 – Koposovetal. (2023), 7 – Erkaletal. (2019a), 8 – Shippetal. (2021), 9 – Correa Magnus & Vasiliev (2022), 10 – Vasilievetal. (2021) and 11 – Peñarrubiaetal. (2016). The outermost literature values are total mass estimates, separatedon the𝑥-axis for visualisation purposes. Quantifying the MW and LMC with SBI13",6.3 The influenceof the LMC on Milky Way mass inference In this sectionwe investigate the importanceof includingan LMC,6.3 The influenceof the LMC on Milky Way mass inference In this sectionwe investigate the importanceof includingan LMC,,,,,"Quantifying the Milky Way, LMC and their interaction using all-sky kinematics of outer halo stars","Richard A. N. Brooks, Jason L. Sanders, Adam M. Dillamore, Nicolás Garavito-Camargo, Vedant Chandra, Adrian M. Price-Whelan, Phillip Cargile",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-09T18:00:04Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.08788v1,2603.08788,galactic_dynamics,111,85,False,False,560,645,False,2.0
